<section class="section--tight">
  <div class="wrap-text">
    <h2>What the lab is like</h2>
    <p>
      The Lab's ethos is to conduct science that sits right at the top of the field, which means
      choosing big questions over safe ones. Thinking big is difficult, but that is what we pride ourselves on.
      We start by reading widely: knowing the classics well enough allows you to identify the great
      unanswered questions; exploring the contemporary literature allows you to identify modern themes, new
      techniques, and exciting new developments. So, we aim high and I promise to always back you!
    </p>
    <p>
      I keep a full lab handbook with all of the information you'll need to be a productive and valued
      member of the Lab, including my mentoring
      commitments to you, and I share it with everyone I invite to interview.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cards">

      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">PhD students</p>
        <h3>Graduate students</h3>
        <p>
          Students join through the School of Biological Sciences at Georgia Tech,
          through <a href="https://biosciences.gatech.edu/phd-biology">Biology</a>, 
          <a href="https://qbios.gatech.edu/apply">Quantitative Biosciences (QBioS)</a>
          , or <a href="https://catalog.gatech.edu/programs/bioinformatics-phd/">Bioinformatics</a>.
          Applications are handled by the graduate programme, but write to me
          before you apply - I only admit people to the lab directly, not via rotations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Tell me what you find interesting and why, what you want to work on, and how that fits into the Lab.
          A short, specific email beats a long, generic one. And make sure you attach a CV!
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">Postdocs</p>
        <h3>Postdoctoral researchers</h3>
        <p>
          I am always glad to hear from prospective postdocs, particularly people
          interested in developing their own line of work within the lab's themes.
          Get in touch early if you are thinking about a fellowship, since the good
          ones close a long way in advance and the proposal is better when we write
          it together.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <p class="card__kicker">Undergraduates</p>
        <h3>Georgia Tech undergraduates</h3>
        <p>
          We take undergraduate researchers every semester, and several have gone
          on to publish and to present at international meetings. If you are a
          Georgia Tech student and this interests you, email me.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap-text">
    <h2>Everyone is welcome here</h2>
    <p>
      Everyone in this lab deserves patience, generosity, and basic kindness.
      Harassment, discrimination, or condescension toward anyone, including
      labmates, collaborators, and the staff and field crews who make our work
      possible, has no place here and will not be tolerated. A team only works
      when people feel safe and valued in it. 
    </p>
    </div>
</section>
